<div>
<h2>When Is the Best Time for Tarpon Fishing?</h2>
<p>For anglers planning specifically around the annual migration, spring through early summer is the key season. The Knowledge Bank identifies this period as the peak migration for Key West tarpon.</p>
<p>That doesn’t mean every day is identical. Tarpon fishing is dynamic. Fish move, conditions change and successful sight fishing depends on visibility and being able to get a presentation in front of the fish.</p>
<p>The overall best time for your trip can also depend on what kind of experience you want. We offer everything from four-hour trips to full days, a dedicated Sunset Tarpon option and a Split Tarpon Trip that divides fishing time between morning and evening.</p>
<p>If tarpon are the main reason you’re coming to Key West, booking ahead is strongly recommended. Key West Pro Guides has a large repeat-customer base along with significant group business, and the prime dates can fill well in advance.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec tint">
<div class="wrap two">
<div>
<h2>Tarpon Fishing Beyond the Migration</h2>
<p>The migration is the centerpiece of the Key West tarpon season, but the fishery is about more than simply putting a month on the calendar.</p>
<p>The real question on any fishing day is what the fish and conditions are doing.</p>
<p>That’s why we don’t promise a catch. We give you an experienced guide, quality equipment and a day built around making the best of current opportunities.</p>
<p>For anglers who are flexible about species, Key West also offers a much broader fishery. Our backcountry trips explore islands, basins, channels, creeks and shallow waters, while other trips target everything from wreck and reef species to offshore pelagics.</p>
<p>If your focus is the Silver King, though, there’s no mistaking why spring and early summer get so much attention.</p>
</div>
